{"duration_api_ms":132732,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"2829e657-be11-4a15-bb80-4872f1aac8fa","total_cost_usd":1.0411981999999997,"usage":{"input_tokens":54,"cache_creation_input_tokens":53940,"cache_read_input_tokens":1904411,"output_tokens":11429,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1530},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":53940,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":83653,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1671,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1671},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":54,"outputTokens":11429,"cacheReadInputTokens":1904411,"cacheCreationInputTokens":53940,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0411981999999997,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1530,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":53940,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":27,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I've added the guards for all five pinned crash paths and flipped the six tagged expectations to match. Both acceptance commands pass: `.theseus/oracle/unit.sh` gives 178 passed and 1 skipped, and `npm run lint:check` exits 0. Commit `862c11b` is on `pkt/PKT-0070`.\n\nOne unit run failed 2 timing tests in `tests/unit/request.tests.js` (300 ms axios timeouts), which has nothing to do with this change. The next two runs passed fully. I recorded it as flaky in the friction line.\n\n**What each guard does (in `DocService/sources/DocsCoServer.js`)**\n- **Connection without handshake:** checked before the handshake URL is read. The server logs \"connection without handshake data\", sends the drop reason and disconnects. The client sees the same result as before, but there's no TypeError now.\n- **`unLockDocument` / `saveChanges` before auth:** ignored, with a warning log. No reply is sent, so nothing new reaches sdkjs and the protocol stays the same.\n- **`startForceSave` with a connection that has no user:** returns early with `UnknownError`, the same reply `forceSaveStart` already gives before auth. Guarding only the user lookup just moved the crash into `converterservice.js`, which is outside the target. That's why the guard sits at the top of `startForceSave`.\n- **User without id:** the server now generates `uid-<timestamp>-<8 hex>` instead of storing the string \"undefined\". The installed web-apps already uses `\"uid-\" + Date.now()` when no user is given, and the random suffix stops two users without ids being merged. I didn't reject these logins, because that would break integrators who leave the id out.\n- **Auth without token or user:** the connection is now refused with access denied and disconnected, instead of being left open and unauthenticated. The untagged \"auth without data.token\" test still passes unchanged.\n\nThe \"auth ignored\" warning that PKT-0064 added isn't on this branch, because PKT-0064 was blocked and never merged. The handling for a missing token or user is therefore written from scratch here.\n\nNo follow-up packets were needed. The friction line and the Executor log are in place, and `theseus validate` reports 0 errors.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas**\n- In docservice, a guard placed on a deep property read can just move the crash further down. Guard at the entry point, then re-run the characterization tests to confirm.\n- The server now generates `uid-…` ids the way web-apps does when a login has no user id.\n- `unit.sh` always runs the whole suite even when given a file filter, so checking a single test file means calling jest directly.","ttft_ms":3806,"type":"result","duration_ms":287660,"uuid":"2b432ba5-f9b4-4a52-8efb-92c04b0a758c","ttft_stream_ms":3127,"time_to_request_ms":420,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":10,"system_prompt":228,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":6,"input_attachments":24,"input_hooks":3,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":8,"init_frame_send":4,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":6,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":3,"request_announcements":20,"query_setup":6,"auto_mode_context_wait":11,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":42,"message_normalization":4,"client_creation":16,"request_build":17},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":142,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":200,"time_to_request_major_faults":27,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":236,"process_anon_mib_result":147,"process_peak_rss_mib":243,"process_cpu_ms_turn":5570,"process_wall_ms_turn":287659,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":1848,"process_wall_ms_streaming":82537,"main_stream_count":27,"main_stream_event_count":1592,"main_stream_chunk_count":1167,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":1848,"wall_ms":82537,"entries":27},"tool":{"cpu_ms":1715,"wall_ms":153433,"entries":26},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":1063,"wall_ms":49980,"entries":27},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":200,"wall_ms":420,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":727,"wall_ms":1267,"entries":26},"after_last_request":{"cpu_ms":17,"wall_ms":22,"entries":1}},"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":9,"cpu_ms":22,"major_f